{"parentUuid":"5d7e6658-4ed7-41fd-9341-a82a6b8beda1","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"03f93166-ecdb-4dfc-baa7-cabff0da5500","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"purring-squishing-blum","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_014GBu5GTbMNsBWxs4hWHnxw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01HxN4auZ6p5ywRsHhQesL5K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/dice-game-scoring.md","content":"# Dice Game Scoring System (ModelOff 2015/2016 Style)\n\n## Scoring Categories\n\n### 1. High and Often\n- **Criteria**: Any turn\n- **Score**: (highest number rolled) × (number of times that highest number appeared)\n\n### 2. Summation\n- **Criteria**: Any turn\n- **Score**: Sum of all six dice rolls\n\n### 3. Highs and Lows\n- **Criteria**: Any turn\n- **Score**: (highest roll) × (lowest roll) × (difference between highest and lowest)\n\n### 4. Only Two Numbers\n- **Criteria**: All six rolls consist of exactly two distinct values\n- **Score**: 30 (flat score)\n- **Example**: 3-6-3-6-6-6\n\n### 5. All the Numbers\n- **Criteria**: Rolls are 1,2,3,4,5,6 in any order\n- **Score**: 40 (flat score)\n\n### 6. Ordered Four\n- **Criteria**: When listed in order rolled, contains a run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers\n- **Score**: 50 (flat score)\n- **Example**: contains subsequence 1-2-3-4 or 5-4-3-2 in the original roll order\n\n## Implementation Pattern\n```python\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef score_turn(rolls):\n    \"\"\"Calculate all possible scores for a turn.\"\"\"\n    scores = {}\n    counts = Counter(rolls)\n    max_val = max(rolls)\n    min_val = min(rolls)\n\n    # High and Often\n    scores['high_often'] = max_val * counts[max_val]\n\n    # Summation\n    scores['summation'] = sum(rolls)\n\n    # Highs and Lows\n    scores['highs_lows'] = max_val * min_val * (max_val - min_val)\n\n    # Only Two Numbers\n    if len(counts) == 2:\n        scores['only_two'] = 30\n\n    # All the Numbers\n    if set(rolls) == {1,2,3,4,5,6}:\n        scores['all_numbers'] = 40\n\n    # Ordered Four (consecutive run of 4 in order rolled)\n    if has_ordered_four(rolls):\n        scores['ordered_four'] = 50\n\n    return scores\n\ndef has_ordered_four(rolls):\n    \"\"\"Check for run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing in original order.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(rolls) - 3):\n        subset = rolls[i:i+4]\n        # Check increasing\n        if all(subset[j+1] == subset[j] + 1 for j in range(3)):\n            return True\n        # Check decreasing\n        if all(subset[j+1] == subset[j] - 1 for j in range(3)):\n            return True\n    return False\n```\n\n## Game Scoring (Optimal Category Assignment)\nEach game has two turns. Score is maximized by choosing the best pair of different categories.\n\n```python\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef best_game_score(turn1_scores, turn2_scores):\n    \"\"\"Find best combined score using different categories for each turn.\"\"\"\n    best = 0\n    for cat1 in turn1_scores:\n        for cat2 in turn2_scores:\n            if cat1 != cat2:\n                combined = turn1_scores[cat1] + turn2_scores[cat2]\n                best = max(best, combined)\n    return best\n```\n\n## Notes on \"Ordered Four\" Interpretation\nThe key phrase is: \"When listed in the order rolled the numbers contain a run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers.\"\n\nThis means checking **contiguous subsequences** of the 6 rolls (as ordered) for 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing values. Check positions [0:4], [1:5], [2:6].\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":48462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":409,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtDwP1HEogwCGrX7gG1y","type":"assistant","uuid":"dde76b3d-ed85-4d34-bf57-1afb9e9e6c48","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:20:06.809Z"}
