{"parentUuid":"dde76b3d-ed85-4d34-bf57-1afb9e9e6c48","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"03f93166-ecdb-4dfc-baa7-cabff0da5500","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"purring-squishing-blum","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01HxN4auZ6p5ywRsHhQesL5K","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/dice-game-scoring.md"}]},"uuid":"c2962838-6720-437f-bb76-d2737b3dc791","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:20:19.660Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/dice-game-scoring.md","content":"# Dice Game Scoring System (ModelOff 2015/2016 Style)\n\n## Scoring Categories\n\n### 1. High and Often\n- **Criteria**: Any turn\n- **Score**: (highest number rolled) × (number of times that highest number appeared)\n\n### 2. Summation\n- **Criteria**: Any turn\n- **Score**: Sum of all six dice rolls\n\n### 3. Highs and Lows\n- **Criteria**: Any turn\n- **Score**: (highest roll) × (lowest roll) × (difference between highest and lowest)\n\n### 4. Only Two Numbers\n- **Criteria**: All six rolls consist of exactly two distinct values\n- **Score**: 30 (flat score)\n- **Example**: 3-6-3-6-6-6\n\n### 5. All the Numbers\n- **Criteria**: Rolls are 1,2,3,4,5,6 in any order\n- **Score**: 40 (flat score)\n\n### 6. Ordered Four\n- **Criteria**: When listed in order rolled, contains a run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers\n- **Score**: 50 (flat score)\n- **Example**: contains subsequence 1-2-3-4 or 5-4-3-2 in the original roll order\n\n## Implementation Pattern\n```python\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef score_turn(rolls):\n    \"\"\"Calculate all possible scores for a turn.\"\"\"\n    scores = {}\n    counts = Counter(rolls)\n    max_val = max(rolls)\n    min_val = min(rolls)\n\n    # High and Often\n    scores['high_often'] = max_val * counts[max_val]\n\n    # Summation\n    scores['summation'] = sum(rolls)\n\n    # Highs and Lows\n    scores['highs_lows'] = max_val * min_val * (max_val - min_val)\n\n    # Only Two Numbers\n    if len(counts) == 2:\n        scores['only_two'] = 30\n\n    # All the Numbers\n    if set(rolls) == {1,2,3,4,5,6}:\n        scores['all_numbers'] = 40\n\n    # Ordered Four (consecutive run of 4 in order rolled)\n    if has_ordered_four(rolls):\n        scores['ordered_four'] = 50\n\n    return scores\n\ndef has_ordered_four(rolls):\n    \"\"\"Check for run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing in original order.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(rolls) - 3):\n        subset = rolls[i:i+4]\n        # Check increasing\n        if all(subset[j+1] == subset[j] + 1 for j in range(3)):\n            return True\n        # Check decreasing\n        if all(subset[j+1] == subset[j] - 1 for j in range(3)):\n            return True\n    return False\n```\n\n## Game Scoring (Optimal Category Assignment)\nEach game has two turns. Score is maximized by choosing the best pair of different categories.\n\n```python\nfrom itertools import product\n\ndef best_game_score(turn1_scores, turn2_scores):\n    \"\"\"Find best combined score using different categories for each turn.\"\"\"\n    best = 0\n    for cat1 in turn1_scores:\n        for cat2 in turn2_scores:\n            if cat1 != cat2:\n                combined = turn1_scores[cat1] + turn2_scores[cat2]\n                best = max(best, combined)\n    return best\n```\n\n## Notes on \"Ordered Four\" Interpretation\nThe key phrase is: \"When listed in the order rolled the numbers contain a run of 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing numbers.\"\n\nThis means checking **contiguous subsequences** of the 6 rolls (as ordered) for 4 consecutive increasing or decreasing values. Check positions [0:4], [1:5], [2:6].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dde76b3d-ed85-4d34-bf57-1afb9e9e6c48"}
{"parentUuid":"6efec8b9-84d2-4da5-8f03-e571b3eee434","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"03f93166-ecdb-4dfc-baa7-cabff0da5500","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"purring-squishing-blum","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01MdkMg9WASzxM2mxiYHd4ut","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/combinatorial-optimization-scoring.md"}]},"uuid":"f382c698-68a3-4c4b-bd26-8bf7074222d3","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:20:19.677Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/combinatorial-optimization-scoring.md","content":"# Combinatorial Optimization for Game Scoring\n\n## Problem\nGiven two turns, each with multiple possible scoring categories, find the optimal assignment of categories to turns such that:\n1. Each turn uses a different category\n2. The combined score is maximized\n\n## Approach: Brute Force (Small Category Sets)\nWith only 6 categories, brute force is efficient:\n\n```python\ndef optimal_game_score(turn1_scores, turn2_scores):\n    \"\"\"\n    turn1_scores: dict of {category: score}\n    turn2_scores: dict of {category: score}\n    Returns the maximum combined score using different categories.\n    \"\"\"\n    best = 0\n    for cat1, score1 in turn1_scores.items():\n        for cat2, score2 in turn2_scores.items():\n            if cat1 != cat2:\n                combined = score1 + score2\n                if combined > best:\n                    best = combined\n    return best\n```\n\n## Player Matching Strategy\nFor the specific question about Player 1 (odd games) vs Player 2 (even games):\n\n```python\n# Games are numbered 1 to 3000\n# Odd games: 1, 3, 5, ..., 2999 -> Player 1\n# Even games: 2, 4, 6, ..., 3000 -> Player 2\n# Matches: game 1 vs game 2, game 3 vs game 4, etc.\n\nplayer1_wins = 0\nplayer2_wins = 0\ndraws = 0\n\nfor i in range(0, len(game_scores), 2):\n    p1_score = game_scores[i]      # odd game (1, 3, 5, ...)\n    p2_score = game_scores[i + 1]  # even game (2, 4, 6, ...)\n    if p1_score > p2_score:\n        player1_wins += 1\n    elif p2_score > p1_score:\n        player2_wins += 1\n    else:\n        draws += 1\n\nanswer = player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n## Complexity\n- 6 categories per turn → max 36 pairs to check per game\n- 3000 games → 108,000 pair checks total\n- Very fast, no optimization needed\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6efec8b9-84d2-4da5-8f03-e571b3eee434"}
{"parentUuid":"933a7a37-0fbb-4bed-93cc-bac937c17b17","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"03f93166-ecdb-4dfc-baa7-cabff0da5500","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"purring-squishing-blum","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_0157hpXxNi9tNhirTA5Jx5QQ","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/pdf-text-extraction.md"}]},"uuid":"fcea80ef-bbcd-4b39-b0f7-ecc544fe712d","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:20:19.693Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/pdf-text-extraction.md","content":"# PDF Text Extraction with Python\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pdfplumber PyPDF2 --break-system-packages\n```\n\n## Using pdfplumber (Recommended)\nBest for structured PDFs with tables and formatted text:\n\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\nwith pdfplumber.open(\"document.pdf\") as pdf:\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        text = page.extract_text()\n        if text:\n            print(text)\n\n        # Extract tables\n        tables = page.extract_tables()\n        for table in tables:\n            for row in table:\n                print(row)\n```\n\n## Using PyPDF2\nSimpler API, good for basic text extraction:\n\n```python\nfrom PyPDF2 import PdfReader\n\nreader = PdfReader(\"document.pdf\")\nfor page in reader.pages:\n    text = page.extract_text()\n    print(text)\n```\n\n## Tips\n- pdfplumber handles complex layouts better than PyPDF2\n- For scanned PDFs, use OCR libraries like pytesseract\n- Always check multiple pages; content may span across pages\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"933a7a37-0fbb-4bed-93cc-bac937c17b17"}
